From cf87d3e489ca627ec568fe5c1a702a53dcd46e02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:51:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] linuxkpi: allow multi-segment dma_map_sg() on
 non-coherent platforms

The LinuxKPI DMA tag is created with nsegments = 1. On a non-coherent
map, busdma bounds the per-map sync list by nsegments, and the count
accumulates across loads into the same map:

	if (map->sync_count == 0 || curaddr != sl_end) {
		if (++map->sync_count > dmat->common.nsegments)
			break;		/* -> EFBIG */

linux_dma_map_sg_attrs() loads every S/G entry into one shared map, so
entry 0 takes the only slot and the first discontiguous entry fails.
dma_map_sg() then returns 0 for any physically scattered list.  Coherent
maps never touch the counter, which is why this only shows up on
non-coherent devices, i.e. most arm64 SoC GPUs.

Seen with drm-kmod and lima (Mali-400) on an Allwinner A64:

	load_phys failed err=27 (EFBIG) i=1/64

on the second entry of every 64-page buffer, surfacing in userland as
EGL_BAD_ALLOC from eglCreateContext.

Raise nsegments to 1024.  It also sizes each map allocation, but the
sync list only grows on a discontiguity, and 1024 entries (32 KiB per
map) cover a fully fragmented 4 MiB list.

Tested on: Allwinner A64 (Banana Pi M64), FreeBSD 15.1 arm64,
drm-kmod + lima, Mesa 26.2.
---
 sys/compat/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_pci.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/compat/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_pci.c b/sys/compat/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_pci.c
index fbfde94..1609be7 100644
--- a/sys/compat/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_pci.c
+++ b/sys/compat/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_pci.c
@@ -223,6 +223,15 @@ linux_pdev_dma_init(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 	return (error);
 }
 
+/*
+ * busdma bounds a non-coherent map's sync list by nsegments, and
+ * linux_dma_map_sg_attrs() loads every S/G entry into one map, so with
+ * nsegments == 1 any physically discontiguous S/G list fails with EFBIG.
+ * The sync list only grows on a discontiguity; 1024 covers a fully
+ * fragmented 4 MiB list.
+ */
+#define	LINUX_DMA_TAG_NSEGMENTS	1024
+
 int
 linux_dma_tag_init(struct device *dev, u64 dma_mask)
 {
@@ -246,7 +255,7 @@ linux_dma_tag_init(struct device *dev, u64 dma_mask)
 	    BUS_SPACE_MAXADDR,		/* highaddr */
 	    NULL, NULL,			/* filtfunc, filtfuncarg */
 	    BUS_SPACE_MAXSIZE,		/* maxsize */
-	    1,				/* nsegments */
+	    LINUX_DMA_TAG_NSEGMENTS,	/* nsegments */
 	    BUS_SPACE_MAXSIZE,		/* maxsegsz */
 	    0,				/* flags */
 	    NULL, NULL,			/* lockfunc, lockfuncarg */
-- 
